# Cursor AI Rules for COSMOVERSE

- You are working on COSMOVERSE, a scientific framework for computational cosmology.
- Maintain rigorous scientific notation and physical units (k in h/Mpc, box in Mpc/h, H0 in km/s/Mpc).
- Never invent cosmological parameters or constants. Use `cosmoverse.core.cosmology.C_KM_S` and `CosmologicalParameters`.
- Ensure periodic boundary conditions for simulations: `np.mod(coords, box_size)`.
- Use Pydantic BaseModel for configuration models and validation.
- All code must pass `uv run pytest`.
- Keep core modules decoupled from hard GPU dependencies (support NumPy/SciPy CPU execution by default).
